#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198018 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198376 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de3fa2fa-304c-583a-8c73-a5ff1db972e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Transformation That Maps a Rectangular Region Onto a Given One"}] :question/id #uuid "87c2cf96-8772-5b28-b6d8-a5616b38543f" :question/math-academy-id "e-12337" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ enclosed in the first quadrant of the $xy$-plane between the curves\n\n$$\ny=x, \\qquad\ny=7x, \\qquad\nx=\\dfrac{3}{y^2}, \\qquad\nx=\\dfrac{5}{y^2}.\n$$\n\nA transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:(u,v) \\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nmaps a rectangular region $\\Delta$ with sides parallel to the $u$- and $v$-axes from the $uv$-plane onto $D$ in the $xy$-plane. Given that\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T} : (u,v) \\to \\Big(\\sqrt[3]{\\dfrac{v}{u^2}}, \\: \\bbox[5pt, white, border: 1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}} \\, \\Big),\n$$\n\nwhat could be the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "We would like to find a rectangular region of the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v\\le d\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u(x,y)\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v(x,y)\\le d\\},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the equations of the left, right, bottom, and top sides are\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}u(x,y)} = a, \\qquad \n{\\color{blue}u(x,y)} = b, \\qquad\n{\\color{red}v(x,y)} = c, \\qquad \n{\\color{red}v(x,y)} = d.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze the boundary of our region $D.$ \n\nRewriting the equations \n\n$$\ny=x, \\qquad\ny=7x, \\qquad\nx=\\dfrac{3}{y^2}, \\qquad\nx=\\dfrac{5}{y^2}\n$$\n\nby moving both variables $x$ and $y$ to the left-hand side, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{x}=1,\\,\\frac{y}{x}=7,\\,x{y}^{2}=3,\\,x{y}^{2}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we put $u(x,y)={\\color{blue}\\dfrac{y}{x}}$ and $v(x,y)={\\color{red}xy^2},$ we can define the transformation $\\mathbf{T}^{-1}$ as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}^{-1} : (x,y) \\to \\left( \\, {\\color{blue}\\dfrac{y}{x}}\\,, \\: \\bbox[2pt, white, border: 1pt solid black]{\\color{red}xy^2} \\right).\n$$\n\nTo find $\\mathbf{T},$ we should express $x$ and $y$ in terms of $u$ and $v.$ Recall that we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}u=\\frac{y}{x} \\\\ v=x{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, $y=ux.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\nv = u^2x^3\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nx^3 = \\dfrac{v}{u^2} \n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nx = \\sqrt[3]{\\dfrac{v}{u^2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x = \\sqrt[3]{\\dfrac{v}{u^2}}$ back into $y=ux,$ we obtain\n\n$$\ny =u\\sqrt[3]{\\dfrac{v}{u^2}} = \\sqrt[3]{uv}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ can be given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T} : (u,v) \\to \\left(\\sqrt[3]{\\dfrac{v}{u^2}}, \\, \\bbox[2pt, white, border: 1pt solid black]{ \\sqrt[3]{uv}} \\right).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198236 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198362 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6d98056-016e-520b-b752-d6a529f2c02d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Rectangular Preimage Given a Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "6d2cd5bf-899f-5b81-9512-ee98489d17ac" :question/math-academy-id "e-7322" :question/problem "Consider the region $D,$ given by\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 2 \\leq \\sqrt{xy} \\leq 4, \\: 2x \\leq y \\leq 3x \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand the transformation $\\mathbf T,$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:(u,v) \\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere $u=\\dfrac{y}{x}$ and $v=xy.$ Find the representation of $\\mathbf{T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $\\mathbf{T}^{-1}(D)$ is the image of $D$ under the action of the transformation $\\mathbf{T}^{-1}.$ \n\nLet's find the image of $\\mathbf{T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane. To do that, we write the region $D$ in terms of $u$ and $v,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}(D) & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le \\sqrt{xy}\\le 4,\\,2x\\le y\\le 3x\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,{2}^{2}\\le (\\sqrt{xy})^{2}\\le {4}^{2},\\,2\\le \\frac{y}{x}\\le 3\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,4\\le xy\\le 16,\\,2\\le \\frac{y}{x}\\le 3\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,4\\le v\\le 16,\\,2\\le u\\le 3\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le u\\le 3,\\,4\\le v\\le 16\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that since $2 \\leq \\sqrt{xy}\\leq 4,$ we must have $x \\neq 0.$ Therefore, $u=\\dfrac{y}{x}$ is well-defined."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198237 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198363 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9156e571-2fe9-5347-95da-c1c97de1a3c9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Transformation That Maps a Region Onto a Type I Region"}] :question/id #uuid "c78f087b-f0e5-58e6-a7a1-92a78c85c4d9" :question/math-academy-id "e-7323" :question/problem "Let $D$ be the finite region bounded by the curve \n$(x+y)^2 + y = 3$ and the line $y=-1.$\nConsider the transformation $\\mathbf T,$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:(u,v) \\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere $u=x+y$ and $v=y.$ Find the representation of $\\mathbf{T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we are given that  \n\n![](images/0d/0da1f765ddb2f8e38296bb80b4e44e1f1489bad06273ee639df1dadca43c35e5.svg)\n\nSubstituting $x+y = u$ and $y = v$ into the equation of the first curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+y)^{2}+y=3\\,⟹\\,{u}^{2}+v=3\\,⟹\\,v=3-{u}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhile substituting $y = v$ into the equation of the second curve, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=-1\\,⟹\\,v=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the intersections of the curves in the $uv$-plane, we solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}v=3-{u}^{2} \\\\ v=-1\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}u=\\pm 2 \\\\ v=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection points are $(\\pm 2, -1).$\n\n![](images/84/84c624aab456b9a090c9c4e6d23c82d8e1f69425050b6f3ee9d4afd18e3f0cec.png)\n\nAs a result, our domain in the $uv$-plane has the type I representation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}^{-1}(D)  = \\big\\{ (u,v) \\: : \\: -2 \\leq u \\leq 2, \\quad  -1 \\leq v \\leq 3-u^2 \\big\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491167 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198362 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6d98056-016e-520b-b752-d6a529f2c02d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Rectangular Preimage Given a Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26fe1bc7-156a-5f71-a9e5-b777e2f5374a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 4,\\,0\\le v\\le 4\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490581} {:answer/id #uuid "60dfb431-d7bd-5434-a387-4e90fb018647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490690} {:answer/id #uuid "9e6fa071-728e-59c3-ade3-633398619359" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490838} {:answer/id #uuid "afd5fd6e-028e-5c45-af5b-c3de243ddfe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 16,\\,0\\le v\\le 2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490860} {:answer/id #uuid "edb9b61e-6a52-53f9-ab53-eaacce9353f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 4\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edb9b61e-6a52-53f9-ab53-eaacce9353f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 4\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490964} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b83bbea-fa13-50a5-b0e6-b4342113702f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491034}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7c6e5eb4-b450-508c-8a0f-3ca8849b044c" :question/math-academy-id "q-103916" :question/problem "Consider the region $D,$ given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le {x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\le 4,\\,0\\le {e}^{xy}\\le 2\\}\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere $u=xy$ and $v={e}^{2xy}.$ Find the representation of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane." :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${T}^{-1}(D)$ is the image of $D$ under the action of the transformation ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nLet's find the image of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane. To do that, we write the region $D$ in terms of $u$ and $v,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}(D) & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le {x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\le 4,\\,0\\le {e}^{xy}\\le 2\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le (xy)^{2}\\le 4,\\,0\\le {({e}^{xy})}^{2}\\le {2}^{2}\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le {u}^{2}\\le 4,\\,0\\le {e}^{2xy}\\le 4\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 4\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that since $0\\le {x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\le 4,$ we must have $-2\\le xy\\ge 2.$ Then, $-2\\le u\\le 2$ too."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491193 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198362 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6d98056-016e-520b-b752-d6a529f2c02d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Rectangular Preimage Given a Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e800195-19a2-5a6e-975c-e82aad24811e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\le u\\le \\frac{1}{2},\\,1\\le v\\le 4\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490539} {:answer/id #uuid "329faad2-95d6-5095-b43a-c93b71443fd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le u\\le 3,\\,2\\le v\\le 16\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490607} {:answer/id #uuid "5e7d820a-3caa-5661-b7b6-9d44f07c407f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\le u\\le \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le v\\le 2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490687} {:answer/id #uuid "74cd4745-47c9-57fc-a48a-128053105122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le u\\le 3,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le v\\le 2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490741} {:answer/id #uuid "9830acdc-aafa-5e94-950b-3fffd465a16e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 2,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\le v\\le 4\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74cd4745-47c9-57fc-a48a-128053105122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le u\\le 3,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le v\\le 2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490741} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c4cd5a1-9c49-53e4-9709-c141685e6eb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491053}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b81d0c3e-2a7e-5a88-b47d-b7de3ec8925d" :question/math-academy-id "q-103933" :question/problem "Consider the region $D,$ given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,2y\\le x\\le 3y,\\,2\\le {4}^{xy}\\le 16\\}\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere $u=\\frac{x}{y}$ and $v=xy.$ Find the representation of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane." :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${T}^{-1}(D)$ is the image of $D$ under the action of the transformation ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nLet's find the image of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane. To do that, we write the region $D$ in terms of $u$ and $v,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}(D) & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2y\\le x\\le 3y,\\,2\\le {4}^{xy}\\le 16\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le \\frac{x}{y}\\le 3,\\,{2}^{1}\\le {2}^{2xy}\\le {2}^{4}\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le u\\le 3,\\,1\\le 2xy\\le 4\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le u\\le 3,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le xy\\le 2\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le u\\le 3,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le v\\le 2\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371464 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198363 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9156e571-2fe9-5347-95da-c1c97de1a3c9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Transformation That Maps a Region Onto a Type I Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b10a777f-8fd9-5577-9d24-0f95dda503a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-3\\le u\\le 3,\\,{u}^{2}\\le v\\le 2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490864} {:answer/id #uuid "b1cabdbf-3361-58d8-b177-2ca0897e54a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\le u\\le \\sqrt{3},\\,2\\le v\\le {u}^{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490866} {:answer/id #uuid "f32b2e89-cfba-5b77-9c8e-ba259cb811b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,2\\le v\\le {u}^{2}-1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490976} {:answer/id #uuid "f7f6d727-e15f-5c25-afca-9277ca9c86b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\le u\\le \\sqrt{3},\\,{u}^{2}-1\\le v\\le 2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490986} {:answer/id #uuid "fd6b7759-c7f6-5950-a91c-3d7fa4f93f86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,{u}^{2}-1\\le v\\le 2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7f6d727-e15f-5c25-afca-9277ca9c86b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\le u\\le \\sqrt{3},\\,{u}^{2}-1\\le v\\le 2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490986} :answer-field/id #uuid "73bf332d-e377-5a51-bb6e-8099852a01ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371465}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "748bffef-751d-5fc9-a40f-bab4bc7c7bcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-103964" :question/problem "Let $D$ be the finite region bounded by the curve \n$(x+{y}^{3})^{2}-y=1$ and the line $y=2.$ Consider the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere $u=x+{y}^{3}$ and $v=y.$ Find the representation of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we are given that \n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x+{y}^{3} \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x+{y}^{3}=u$ and $y=v$ into the equation of the first curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+{y}^{3})^{2}-y=1\\,⟹\\,{u}^{2}-v=1\\,⟹\\,v={u}^{2}-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhile substituting $y=v$ into the equation of the second curve, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=2\\,⟹\\,v=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the intersections of the curves in the $uv$-plane, we solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}v={u}^{2}-1 \\\\ v=2\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}u=\\pm \\sqrt{3} \\\\ v=2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection points are $(\\pm \\sqrt{3},2).$\n\n![](images/fc/fc6e896f50255deea574c52014935097b6c0b49aa6a1e54a9d6a484dc1b8cc61.png)\n\nAs a result, our domain in the $uv$-plane has the type I representation \n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}(D)=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\le u\\le \\sqrt{3},\\,{u}^{2}-1\\le v\\le 2\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491144 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198363 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9156e571-2fe9-5347-95da-c1c97de1a3c9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Transformation That Maps a Region Onto a Type I Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23d06fa1-4432-58d7-aa6e-761d11632e35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 2,\\,{u}^{2}-5\\le v\\le 4\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490576} {:answer/id #uuid "35610698-c817-574b-bdf4-ec8a6ffda956" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-\\sqrt{5}\\le u\\le \\sqrt{5},\\,4\\le v\\le {u}^{2}+5\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490612} {:answer/id #uuid "40c5e994-bcd5-5048-b3d1-b99b08966149" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-\\sqrt{5}\\le u\\le \\sqrt{5},\\,4\\le v\\le {u}^{2}-5\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490636} {:answer/id #uuid "b62ad7a7-28c3-5dc3-a717-9830f6638635" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-3\\le u\\le 3,\\,4\\le v\\le {u}^{2}+5\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490874} {:answer/id #uuid "d8c7380d-be45-5611-a6e6-e1b2df54f359" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-3\\le u\\le 3,\\,{u}^{2}-5\\le v\\le 4\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8c7380d-be45-5611-a6e6-e1b2df54f359" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-3\\le u\\le 3,\\,{u}^{2}-5\\le v\\le 4\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490923} :answer-field/id #uuid "7acd4456-5770-5138-ba6b-df1d44fe804e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4efc1305-a064-5e20-8b2c-ca7aa38971ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-103966" :question/problem "Let $D$ be the finite region bounded by the curve \n$y-{({y}^{2}+\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}=-5$ and the line $y=4.$ Consider the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere $u={y}^{2}+\\frac{x}{2}$ and $v=y.$ Find the representation of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we are given that \n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}+\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{2}+\\frac{x}{2}=u$ and $y=v$ into the equation of the first curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{({y}^{2}+\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}=-5\\,⟹\\,v-{u}^{2}=-5\\,⟹\\,v={u}^{2}-5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhile substituting $y=v$ into the equation of the second curve, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=4\\,⟹\\,v=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the intersections of the curves in the $uv$-plane, we solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}v={u}^{2}-5 \\\\ v=4\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}u=\\pm 3 \\\\ v=4.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection points are $(\\pm 3,4).$\n\n![](images/fe/fe39efb538d3270028fa5892402d56a8ae0e061968ecca8c676d8ad9f482644e.png)\n\nAs a result, our domain in the $uv$-plane has the type I representation \n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}(D)=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-3\\le u\\le 3,\\,{u}^{2}-5\\le v\\le 4\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491164 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198363 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9156e571-2fe9-5347-95da-c1c97de1a3c9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Transformation That Maps a Region Onto a Type I Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19abb226-9eda-5d7f-9822-cc133978f742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1-{u}^{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490560} {:answer/id #uuid "6fc046b9-4185-52db-ae91-ccacbdea4053" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 2,\\,{u}^{2}-3\\le v\\le 0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490731} {:answer/id #uuid "8c2aa9ec-3898-53a7-bef3-47bfcb56b6ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 3+{u}^{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490791} {:answer/id #uuid "97d4fc2f-1df9-58b2-950e-29e42310ba35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,{u}^{2}-1\\le v\\le 0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490820} {:answer/id #uuid "dab0bc01-6b41-5e50-9c41-587e6d2456a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 0,\\,{u}^{2}-1\\le v\\le 2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97d4fc2f-1df9-58b2-950e-29e42310ba35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,{u}^{2}-1\\le v\\le 0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490820} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a6234f6-a5c9-5830-8063-1c706e48d85a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491044}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "77327bb6-1e9a-5178-984c-098fa761c5e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-103977" :question/problem "Let $D$ be the finite region bounded by the curve \n$({x}^{3}+y)^{2}+y=3$ and the line $y=2.$ Consider the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere $u={x}^{3}+y$ and $v=2-y.$ Find the representation of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we are given that \n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+y \\\\ 2-y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}^{3}+y=u$ and $y=2-v$ into the equation of the first curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{3}+y)^{2}+y=3\\,⟹\\,{u}^{2}+2-v=3\\,⟹\\,v={u}^{2}-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhile substituting $y=2-v$ into the equation of the second curve, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=2\\,⟹\\,2-v=2\\,⟹\\,v=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the intersections of the curves in the $uv$-plane, we solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}v={u}^{2}-1 \\\\ v=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}u=\\pm 1 \\\\ v=0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection points are $(\\pm 1,0).$\n\n![](images/60/60d8d3e30eba31683d1b6bb9bf399aa20f2bda37be1cb31bec431a4e27c0f54e.png)\n\nAs a result, our domain in the $uv$-plane has the type I representation \n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}(D)=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,{u}^{2}-1\\le v\\le 0\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491169 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198376 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de3fa2fa-304c-583a-8c73-a5ff1db972e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Transformation That Maps a Rectangular Region Onto a Given One"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "522aae33-8182-5b30-8e8e-afea54ee6b02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490668} {:answer/id #uuid "94810c8b-9e6a-5224-9b38-6f5dee82fb4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490813} {:answer/id #uuid "c3c98166-8381-5b45-9140-6503fe34ef44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490887} {:answer/id #uuid "d712910a-d224-5141-b66d-db3f680262d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490917} {:answer/id #uuid "eb5057e9-1c3b-569f-97d5-0556deaf27bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x-2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94810c8b-9e6a-5224-9b38-6f5dee82fb4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490813} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b27d171-aaec-5efc-8b33-98ff913947bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491039}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7fe852c9-f9c5-516e-be6d-ac44e221645a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161074" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ enclosed in the first quadrant of the $xy$-plane between the lines and curves\n\n$$\n2y=x+1,\\,2y=x+3,\\,y=\\frac{1}{x},\\,y=\\frac{5}{x}.\n$$\n\nA transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nmaps a rectangular region $Δ$ with sides parallel to the $u$- and $v$-axes from the $uv$-plane onto $D$ in the $xy$-plane. Given that\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:(x,y)\\to (\\,\\bbox[5pt,white,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}}\\,,\\,xy),\n$$\n\nwhat could be the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "We would like to find a rectangular region of the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v\\le d\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u(x,y)\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v(x,y)\\le d\\},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the equations of the left, right, bottom, and top sides are\n\n$$\nu(x,y)=a,\\,u(x,y)=b,\\,v(x,y)=c,\\,v(x,y)=d.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze the boundary of our region $D.$ \n\nRe-writing the equations \n\n$$\n2y=x+1,\\,2y=x+3,\\,y=\\frac{1}{x},\\,y=\\frac{5}{x}\n$$\n\nby moving both variables $x$ and $y$ to the left-hand side, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y-x=1,\\,2y-x=3,\\,xy=1,\\,xy=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we put $u(x,y)=2y-x$ and $v(x,y)=xy,$ we can define the transformation ${T}^{-1}$ as\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:(x,y)\\to (\\,2y-x\\,,\\,xy).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371920 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198376 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de3fa2fa-304c-583a-8c73-a5ff1db972e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Transformation That Maps a Rectangular Region Onto a Given One"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8b25d0f-d59c-57b3-a596-094a2fa26bca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371922} {:answer/id #uuid "72883a1f-03e8-59d7-9c1e-67e9d5900697" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{e}^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371923} {:answer/id #uuid "76c28201-1240-5f72-87b6-49c31ffb6add" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371924} {:answer/id #uuid "2c5d9b6c-780b-50a0-b459-dab290b52433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371925} {:answer/id #uuid "9774e3c6-8463-5669-9931-9ec714e68ea1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9774e3c6-8463-5669-9931-9ec714e68ea1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371926} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec49a288-bd93-5fe5-8569-21989622da29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ec93a22b-8046-55ff-bd79-1effdf7c3586" :question/math-academy-id "q-161075" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ enclosed in the first quadrant of the $xy$-plane between the curves\n\n$$\n{e}^{x}=\\frac{1}{y},\\,{e}^{x}=\\frac{3}{y},\\,y=x,\\,y=\\frac{x}{3}.\n$$\n\nA transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nmaps a rectangular region $Δ$ with sides parallel to the $u$- and $v$-axes from the $uv$-plane onto $D$ in the $xy$-plane. Given that\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:(x,y)\\to (\\,\\bbox[5pt,white,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}}\\,,\\,\\frac{x}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhat could be the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "We would like to find a rectangular region of the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v\\le d\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u(x,y)\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v(x,y)\\le d\\},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the equations of the left, right, bottom, and top sides are\n\n$$\nu(x,y)=a,\\,u(x,y)=b,\\,v(x,y)=c,\\,v(x,y)=d.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze the boundary of our region $D.$ \n\nRe-writing the equations \n\n$$\n{e}^{x}=\\frac{1}{y},\\,{e}^{x}=\\frac{3}{y},\\,y=x,\\,y=\\frac{x}{3}\n$$\n\nby moving both variables $x$ and $y$ to the left-hand side, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}y=1,\\,{e}^{x}y=3,\\,\\frac{x}{y}=1,\\,\\frac{x}{y}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we put $u(x,y)={e}^{x}y$ and $v(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y},$ we can define the transformation ${T}^{-1}$ as\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:(x,y)\\to (\\,{e}^{x}y\\,,\\,\\frac{x}{y}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198376 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de3fa2fa-304c-583a-8c73-a5ff1db972e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Transformation That Maps a Rectangular Region Onto a Given One"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6175d253-803e-5e5c-8ea5-14c5a35fd99f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490692} {:answer/id #uuid "7470d346-73d8-5ae5-ac4d-328a43365050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490740} {:answer/id #uuid "83a181b2-4397-5fab-8d3a-a09ac1c75bdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490777} {:answer/id #uuid "c9182d6e-5712-5a77-b82d-7806fc04680b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490893} {:answer/id #uuid "de7c56d7-5a73-54e5-9bc9-b50b5766ca59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7470d346-73d8-5ae5-ac4d-328a43365050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490740} :answer-field/id #uuid "d25989c9-ac7b-5cae-ab6b-b2623e213802" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491086}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f19d953d-521c-5438-8b80-3660f96df807" :question/math-academy-id "q-161082" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ enclosed in the first quadrant of the $xy$-plane between the curves and lines\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}},\\,y=\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}},\\,y=x+2,\\,y=x+7.\n$$\n\nA transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nmaps a rectangular region $Δ$ with sides parallel to the $u$- and $v$-axes from the $uv$-plane onto $D$ in the $xy$-plane. Given that\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:(x,y)\\to ({x}^{2}y\\,,\\,\\bbox[5pt,white,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhat could be the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "We would like to find a rectangular region of the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v\\le d\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u(x,y)\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v(x,y)\\le d\\},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the equations of the left, right, bottom, and top sides are\n\n$$\nu(x,y)=a,\\,u(x,y)=b,\\,v(x,y)=c,\\,v(x,y)=d.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze the boundary of our region $D.$ \n\nRe-writing the equations \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}},\\,y=\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}},\\,y=x+2,\\,y=x+7\n$$\n\nby moving both variables $x$ and $y$ to the left-hand side, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}y=2,\\,{x}^{2}y=7,\\,y-x=2,\\,y-x=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we put $u(x,y)={x}^{2}y$ and $v(x,y)=y-x,$ we can define the transformation ${T}^{-1}$ as\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:(x,y)\\to (\\,{x}^{2}y\\,,\\,y-x).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371934 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198376 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de3fa2fa-304c-583a-8c73-a5ff1db972e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Transformation That Maps a Rectangular Region Onto a Given One"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74b34730-5f02-5098-b7fb-5232e115371e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{v}{u}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371936} {:answer/id #uuid "8a25546c-4c65-59a2-ae10-fee6212f690a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{v}{{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371937} {:answer/id #uuid "075c05d5-a6f6-5297-a443-b88b0dfc4257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{v}{{u}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371938} {:answer/id #uuid "e16013ed-3259-5a37-ac71-ba1971f865e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{v}{u}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371939} {:answer/id #uuid "84d7448b-2caf-5eb4-9943-32338791b4c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{{v}^{2}}{u}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74b34730-5f02-5098-b7fb-5232e115371e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{v}{u}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371936} :answer-field/id #uuid "38d2aefd-cac0-5e58-981d-4b55d8b67a4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "21e23291-6559-5eea-9b70-7fd00996880f" :question/math-academy-id "q-161085" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ enclosed in the first quadrant of the $xy$-plane between the curves\n\n$$\nx=y,\\,x=5y,\\,x=\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}},\\,x=\\frac{7}{{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nA transformation $T,$ where\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nmaps a rectangular region $Δ$ with sides parallel to the $u$- and $v$-axes from the $uv$-plane onto $D$ in the $xy$-plane. Given that\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{2}v},\\,\\bbox[5pt,white,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhat could be the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "We would like to find a rectangular region of the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v\\le d\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u(x,y)\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v(x,y)\\le d\\},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the equations of the left, right, bottom, and top sides are\n\n$$\nu(x,y)=a,\\,u(x,y)=b,\\,v(x,y)=c,\\,v(x,y)=d.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze the boundary of our region $D.$ \n\nRewriting the equations \n\n$$\nx=y,\\,x=5y,\\,x=\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}},\\,x=\\frac{7}{{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nby moving both variables $x$ and $y$ to the left-hand side, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{y}=1,\\,\\frac{x}{y}=5,\\,x{y}^{2}=2,\\,x{y}^{2}=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we put $u(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y}$ and $v(x,y)=x{y}^{2},$ we can define the transformation ${T}^{-1}$ as\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:(x,y)\\to (\\,\\frac{x}{y}\\,,\\,x{y}^{2}).\n$$\n\nTo find $T,$ we should express $x$ and $y$ in terms of $u$ and $v.$ Recall that we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}u=\\frac{x}{y} \\\\ v=x{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, $x=uy.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\nv=u{y}^{3}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{3}=\\frac{v}{u}\\,⟹\\,y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{v}{u}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{v}{u}}$ back into $x=uy,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nx=u\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{v}{u}}=\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{2}v}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the transformation $T$ can be given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{2}v},\\,\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{v}{u}}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491130 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198376 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de3fa2fa-304c-583a-8c73-a5ff1db972e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Transformation That Maps a Rectangular Region Onto a Given One"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "045f0275-d1e4-5b27-b5f6-8d4e45ec696c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{2}{v}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490521} {:answer/id #uuid "5593f5ff-b58e-55d4-a9a0-95f4cbc14195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{2}v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490672} {:answer/id #uuid "5d8f38f5-e90c-5a2b-8edd-e10b4a3588aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{u{v}^{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490685} {:answer/id #uuid "7293d5b5-ff63-5e3f-8a5f-131c428aa135" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{u}^{2}v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490737} {:answer/id #uuid "d4d5d88c-4349-526a-92c5-12025b9a4513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{u{v}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5593f5ff-b58e-55d4-a9a0-95f4cbc14195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{2}v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490672} :answer-field/id #uuid "18381e39-1eee-5868-bf94-1f26e7c134e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491013}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2ef3f070-3842-5746-bbe4-723d2d023508" :question/math-academy-id "q-161088" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ enclosed in the first quadrant of the $xy$-plane between the curves\n\n$$\nx=3y,\\,x=7y,\\,x=\\frac{4}{{y}^{2}},\\,x=\\frac{9}{{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nA transformation $T,$ where\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nmaps a rectangular region $Δ$ with sides parallel to the $u$- and $v$-axes from the $uv$-plane onto $D$ in the $xy$-plane. Given that\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (\\,\\bbox[5pt,white,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}}\\,,\\,\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{v}{u}}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhat could be the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "We would like to find a rectangular region of the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v\\le d\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u(x,y)\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v(x,y)\\le d\\},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the equations of the left, right, bottom, and top sides are\n\n$$\nu(x,y)=a,\\,u(x,y)=b,\\,v(x,y)=c,\\,v(x,y)=d.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze the boundary of our region $D.$ \n\nRewriting the equations \n\n$$\nx=3y,\\,x=7y,\\,x=\\frac{4}{{y}^{2}},\\,x=\\frac{9}{{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nby moving both variables $x$ and $y$ to the left-hand side, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{y}=3,\\,\\frac{x}{y}=7,\\,x{y}^{2}=4,\\,x{y}^{2}=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we put $u(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y}$ and $v(x,y)=x{y}^{2},$ we can define the transformation ${T}^{-1}$ as\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:(x,y)\\to (\\,\\frac{x}{y}\\,,\\,x{y}^{2}).\n$$\n\nTo find $T,$ we should express $x$ and $y$ in terms of $u$ and $v.$ Recall that we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}u=\\frac{x}{y} \\\\ v=x{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, $x=uy.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\nv=u{y}^{3}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{3}=\\frac{v}{u}\\,⟹\\,y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{v}{u}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{v}{u}}$ back into $x=uy,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nx=u\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{v}{u}}=\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{2}v}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the transformation $T$ can be given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{2}v},\\,\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{v}{u}}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491196 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198362 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6d98056-016e-520b-b752-d6a529f2c02d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Rectangular Preimage Given a Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "686f0f45-4268-55ae-b115-6fcc6b376e23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u+v\\le 3,\\,-4\\le v-u\\le -1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490708} {:answer/id #uuid "6f8c4139-3adc-522c-a972-1f57bfd7c50f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 3,\\,-4\\le v\\le -1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490730} {:answer/id #uuid "81c1be48-577d-5d97-a6b7-4c5839af08b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 4,\\,-4\\le v\\le -1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490772} {:answer/id #uuid "c643b804-bec3-521c-b865-c886f5447176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u+v\\le 4,\\,-4\\le v-u\\le -1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490891} {:answer/id #uuid "ee28c4af-a780-585b-8105-332bde03ab60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 4,\\,-4\\le v\\le -1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81c1be48-577d-5d97-a6b7-4c5839af08b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 4,\\,-4\\le v\\le -1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490772} :answer-field/id #uuid "1af41890-dfcd-525f-b198-d2450be576b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c625d289-ee92-5b87-a0d1-89bb85d080fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-83634" :question/problem "Consider the region $D,$ given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x+y\\le 3,\\,-4\\le y-x\\le -1\\}\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere $u=x+y+1$ and $v=y-x.$ Find the representation of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane." :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${T}^{-1}(D)$ is the image of $D$ under the action of the transformation ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nLet's find the image of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane. To do that, we write the region $D$ in terms of $u$ and $v,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}(D) & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le x+y\\le 3,\\,-4\\le y-x\\le -1\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le (x+y)+1\\le 4,\\,-4\\le y-x\\le -1\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 4,\\,-4\\le v\\le -1\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491173 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198363 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9156e571-2fe9-5347-95da-c1c97de1a3c9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Transformation That Maps a Region Onto a Type I Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68175394-e4ca-5d10-ab4c-d0b4ad11a632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-3\\le u\\le 3,\\,{u}^{4}-2\\le v\\le 2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490707} {:answer/id #uuid "7e893f29-7887-55f5-b232-130daab050d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-\\sqrt[4]{3}\\le u\\le \\sqrt[4]{3},\\,{u}^{4}\\le v\\le 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490762} {:answer/id #uuid "8f1c659d-2ed5-5423-ba2c-4e1db51a5c08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-\\sqrt[4]{3}\\le u\\le \\sqrt[4]{3},\\,{u}^{4}-1\\le v\\le 2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490799} {:answer/id #uuid "928bc095-278f-58c6-a0a7-bb128d861290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,{u}^{4}-1\\le v\\le 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490807} {:answer/id #uuid "a906c089-2e94-5bfc-916c-2d334da95157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-\\sqrt[4]{2}\\le u\\le \\sqrt[4]{2},\\,{u}^{4}-2\\le v\\le 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f1c659d-2ed5-5423-ba2c-4e1db51a5c08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-\\sqrt[4]{3}\\le u\\le \\sqrt[4]{3},\\,{u}^{4}-1\\le v\\le 2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490799} :answer-field/id #uuid "b78bc637-cc83-5978-b813-6627b4377d72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491075}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8586cda1-86eb-51fb-b15b-c80e0240542a" :question/math-academy-id "q-83638" :question/problem "Let $D$ be the finite region bounded by the curve \n$({x}^{3}-y)^{4}-y=1$ and the line $y=2.$ Consider the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere $u={x}^{3}-y$ and $v=y.$ Find the representation of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we are given that \n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}^{3}-y=u$ and $y=v$ into the equation of the first curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{3}-y)^{4}-y=1\\,⟹\\,{u}^{4}-v=1\\,⟹\\,v={u}^{4}-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhile substituting $y=v$ into the equation of the second curve, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=2\\,⟹\\,v=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the intersections of the curves in the $uv$-plane, we solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}v={u}^{4}-1 \\\\ v=2\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}u=\\pm \\sqrt[4]{3} \\\\ v=2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection points are $(\\pm \\sqrt[4]{3},2).$\n\n![](images/5a/5a2e3fd6f3669f38834359f69e68b01a1e0d1438023418c5234d4071182f4808.png)\n\nAs a result, our domain in the $uv$-plane has the type I representation \n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}(D)=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-\\sqrt[4]{3}\\le u\\le \\sqrt[4]{3},\\,{u}^{4}-1\\le v\\le 2\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491121 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198362 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6d98056-016e-520b-b752-d6a529f2c02d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Rectangular Preimage Given a Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b51cb89-8057-5b8d-b8d5-ffcd6be96524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 5,\\,2\\le v\\le e\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490528} {:answer/id #uuid "4903fa3b-9718-539b-8c4b-baba19dae8a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le u\\le 5,\\,1\\le v\\le {e}^{x}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490649} {:answer/id #uuid "497231f8-7095-506a-a075-dba7c325fad2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le u\\le 5,\\,1\\le v\\le e\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490650} {:answer/id #uuid "6a6b0a54-c65d-57cf-b63a-56831cf7f3e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le u\\le e,\\,1\\le v\\le 5\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490715} {:answer/id #uuid "947bb16a-93b1-5848-829d-bbd0b7dd5972" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,e\\le u\\le 5,\\,-2\\le v\\le {e}^{x}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "497231f8-7095-506a-a075-dba7c325fad2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le u\\le 5,\\,1\\le v\\le e\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490650} :answer-field/id #uuid "0197c098-7e4d-5348-9088-e2f7a5c3cca1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "171517bd-e706-5408-b35c-f81cec428f88" :question/math-academy-id "q-85305" :question/problem "Consider the region $D,$ given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)\\le 1,\\,2{e}^{x}\\le y\\le 5{e}^{x}\\}\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere $u=\\frac{y}{{e}^{x}}$ and $v=x-2y.$ Find the representation of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane." :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${T}^{-1}(D)$ is the image of $D$ under the action of the transformation ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nLet's find the image of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane. To do that, we write the region $D$ in terms of $u$ and $v,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}(D) & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)\\le 1,\\,2{e}^{x}\\le y\\le 5{e}^{x}\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,{e}^{0}\\le {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)}\\le {e}^{1},\\,\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{{e}^{x}}\\le \\frac{y}{{e}^{x}}\\le \\frac{5{e}^{x}}{{e}^{x}}\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le x-2y\\le e,\\,2\\le \\frac{y}{{e}^{x}}\\le 5\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le v\\le e,\\,2\\le u\\le 5\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le u\\le 5,\\,1\\le v\\le e\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491131 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198362 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6d98056-016e-520b-b752-d6a529f2c02d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Rectangular Preimage Given a Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "115b7cbb-135f-5386-a258-4bc135482725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 2\\sqrt{2},\\,1\\le v\\le 32\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490548} {:answer/id #uuid "1b527067-71e5-5782-8350-3866b45c0125" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le \\sqrt{3},\\,2\\le v\\le 32\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490561} {:answer/id #uuid "50a5909b-b79b-5a4b-939c-42acf9f14a6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 3,\\,0\\le v\\le 16\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490666} {:answer/id #uuid "d53e68ec-8f36-536f-af07-a950bc9a9250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 32\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490914} {:answer/id #uuid "d77e5b62-67a2-5236-bc0f-7d9a7a861c1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 2,\\,2\\le v\\le 3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d53e68ec-8f36-536f-af07-a950bc9a9250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 32\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490914} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e9f3836-0c23-5281-8b2b-df9e0e832e0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491018}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "308c3b1f-dc69-5e5d-ac0f-cca362b4ad91" :question/math-academy-id "q-85306" :question/problem "Consider the region $D,$ given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le {e}^{3y}\\le 8,\\,0\\le {e}^{x/5}\\le 2\\}\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere $u={e}^{y}$ and $v={e}^{x}.$ Find the representation of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane." :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${T}^{-1}(D)$ is the image of $D$ under the action of the transformation ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nLet's find the image of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane. To do that, we write the region $D$ in terms of $u$ and $v,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}(D) & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le {e}^{3y}\\le 8,\\,0\\le {e}^{x/5}\\le 2\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le {({e}^{y})}^{3}\\le 8,\\,0\\le {({e}^{x})}^{1/5}\\le 2\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,\\sqrt[3]{1}\\le \\sqrt[3]{{({e}^{y})}^{3}}\\le \\sqrt[3]{8},\\,{0}^{5}\\le {({({e}^{x})}^{1/5})}^{5}\\le {2}^{5}\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le {e}^{y}\\le 2,\\,0\\le {e}^{x}\\le 32\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 32\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373374 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198363 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9156e571-2fe9-5347-95da-c1c97de1a3c9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Transformation That Maps a Region Onto a Type I Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2aa2f646-395b-5b75-a787-d20141b1a4db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 0,\\,u\\le v\\le {u}^{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490595} {:answer/id #uuid "33cd4fc6-c261-5b2f-815e-d27c080b9c91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,-{u}^{2}\\le v\\le u\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490610} {:answer/id #uuid "9a14f4a9-ddff-5f20-806d-a37f282b6766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 0,\\,{u}^{2}\\le v\\le u\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490829} {:answer/id #uuid "a3c57f78-9786-5451-977c-b103be878303" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,-u\\le v\\le {u}^{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490847} {:answer/id #uuid "d439b385-9372-55c9-8591-509fcbffd3a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 0,\\,u\\le v\\le -{u}^{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d439b385-9372-55c9-8591-509fcbffd3a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 0,\\,u\\le v\\le -{u}^{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490912} :answer-field/id #uuid "23350df3-f523-5ba3-82a1-2c19d5fe91f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373375}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bb3932ad-6398-5142-9ae7-9ead5c34792e" :question/math-academy-id "q-85314" :question/problem "Let $D$ be the finite region bounded by the curve \n$(x-y)^{2}+x+y=0$ and  the line $y=0.$ \nConsider the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere $u=x-y$ and $v=x+y.$ Find the representation of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we are given that \n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x-y \\\\ x+y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x-y=u$ and $x+y=v$ into the equation of the first curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-y)^{2}+x+y=0\\,⟹\\,(x-y)^{2}+(x+y)=0\\,⟹\\,v=-{u}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y=u \\\\ x+y=v\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,y=\\frac{v-u}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this value into the equation of the given line yields:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=0\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{v-u}{2}=0 & \\,⟹\\,v=u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, to find the intersections of the resulting lines in the $uv$-plane, we solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}v=-{u}^{2} \\\\ v=u\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}u(u+1)=0 \\\\ v=u.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection points are $(0,0)$ and $(-1,-1).$ \n\n![](images/05/05d7e65dca3c6d116d01be9e57fc83f3e3edcda4135a3f96fea82af8db4f2d1e.png)\n\nAs a result, our domain in the $uv$-plane has the type I representation \n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}(D)=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 0,\\,u\\le v\\le -{u}^{2}\\}.\n$$"}]}
